cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below."
title: "SEAM: Detecting Right-Answer, Wrong-Reason Behavior in Open-Weight Reasoning Models"
abstract: >-
  An open benchmark of 195 reasoning problems, each in three matched variants
  (clean, hinted, and misleadingly hinted), for studying right-answer /
  wrong-reason behaviour in open-weight reasoning models.
authors:
  - name: "The SEAM Authors"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-06-04"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - interpretability
  - reasoning
  - large-language-models
  - benchmark
  - chain-of-thought
  - shortcut-learning
